# fresh_res_info_while_kernel_held: InfoIndirect (69) behind an exec whose kernel runs for 13 s.  The exec runs fresh_res_spin as fixed work: 220,000 polls of a word the guest leaves 0, 13.1 s on the reference host alone and only longer under load, far past the 5 s below. 69 follows on the same FIFO, in the same doorbell.  In process (blocks, map), 69 waits at most 5 s for the FIFO event, which only the exec's completion signals, then reports status 3 (`waitUntilSignaledValue:timeoutMS:5000`): a fault. Nothing is published while the kernel runs, not even that fault (the checkpoint at 8 s): the fault is published only after the exec's stamp, once the kernel has ended (pump: a stamp behind an unsignalled one waits).  With isolation, the service's exec signals the FIFO event when its command buffer is scheduled (`encodeSignalEventScheduled`), not when it completes, so the service's 5 s wait is met at once and 69 completes; its stamp still follows the exec's. docs/testing.md 7.4 listed this timeout as needing a GPU hang: a guest kernel that runs past 5 s is enough.
